120 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (FedEx selected the Unit Load Device \(ULD\) optimization problem for the Inter IIT Tech Meet 13.0 due to its potential to significantly enhance operational efficiency, reduce costs, and improve service reliability across its logistics network. ULDs are standardized containers used in air shipments, varying in shape and size, and have strict weight and volume limits. Properly packing these devices ensures efficient use of space, minimizes costs, and guarantees that Priority Packages, which are of higher precedence, are shipped without delay. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
121 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The challenge is to decide which packages to load into which ULDs, while considering the weight limits, package dimensions, and ensuring that Priority Packages are not compromised.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
122 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The optimization of ULD packing offers several key benefits to the logistics industry. First, it increases efficiency by maximizing the available space in each ULD, allowing more goods to be transported per flight. This reduces the number of shipments required and leads to better resource utilization. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
