125 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (By reducing the number of ULDs needed, operational costs, such as fuel, labor, and handling fees, are significantly lowered. Fewer ULDs also mean less storage and transportation costs, directly impacting the bottom line.)
/E (By reducing the number of ULDs needed, operational costs, such as fuel, labor, and handling fees, are significantly lowered. Fewer ULDs also mean less storage and transportation costs, directly impacting the bottom line.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
126 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (In addition to cost savings, ULD optimization improves timeliness. Properly packed ULDs ensure that no packages, especially Priority Packages, are left behind, resulting in faster delivery times. This is especially crucial for time-sensitive shipments, improving customer satisfaction and overall service reliability. )
/E (In addition to cost savings, ULD optimization improves timeliness. Properly packed ULDs ensure that no packages, especially Priority Packages, are left behind, resulting in faster delivery times. This is especially crucial for time-sensitive shipments, improving customer satisfaction and overall service reliability. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Moreover, efficient ULD usage leads to higher profitability. By handling more shipments per trip without significantly increasing costs, logistics companies can generate additional revenue. Furthermore, optimizing the use of ULDs reduces inefficiencies, directly benefiting the company's financial performance.)
/E (Moreover, efficient ULD usage leads to higher profitability. By handling more shipments per trip without significantly increasing costs, logistics companies can generate additional revenue. Furthermore, optimizing the use of ULDs reduces inefficiencies, directly benefiting the company's financial performance.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
