<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The packages that are being transported are usually stacked inside large standard sized containers, called Unit Load Devices \(ULDs\), that are then loaded onto the aircraft.  These ULDs are available in various standard sizes, meant for carrying different types and quantities of packages. Each of them have specific shapes, dimensions, weight, volume and a limit for how much load they can carry. Some of the varieties of ULDs are shown in the pictures below:)
/E (The packages that are being transported are usually stacked inside large standard sized containers, called Unit Load Devices \(ULDs\), that are then loaded onto the aircraft.  These ULDs are available in various standard sizes, meant for carrying different types and quantities of packages. Each of them have specific shapes, dimensions, weight, volume and a limit for how much load they can carry. Some of the varieties of ULDs are shown in the pictures below:)
/Alt ()
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
